AcpFlow retains one prompt/cancel, two engine events, two finite connection
replies and writer capacity 0..2 standing for 256. EngineNeverWaits is the
enabledness of that real emit guard, with updates inside their declared bounds;
nonvacuity checks actual graph edges at full capacity. Existing fairness for
admission/engine/projection/writer/resume is retained.
McpGroupClose has 8 correct states and 12 broken states. It abstracts grace
expiry and group SIGKILL delivery as one transition, followed by leader reap.
Kernel signal delivery, timing and ESRCH/reaping remain real process witnesses.
Group ownership and pgid reuse remain in HarnessProcessLifecycle. The MCP
server's startup/generation/timeout contract remains HarnessMcpServer.
Durable prompt admission in AcpFlow abstracts the implementation's replay;
actual queue overflow and held-EOF recovery are the direct unit witness.
No arbitrary Rust refinement or unrestricted TLC replacement is claimed.

